**Read:** [Multizone airflow and contaminants — Dols and Polidoro, CONTAM 3.4](../sources/CONTAM-Multizone-Airflow-and-Contaminants-NIST.lingua#r_5HECDC480RSYAJ3SQ2QNFHCN46), complete theory and a worked application; [Door motion, human movement and aerosol exchange — Zheng and colleagues](../sources/Door-Motion-Human-Movement-and-Aerosol-Exchange-Zheng.lingua#r_7CWNYE36WG4XSVT18MFMZRV1DH) in full; [Sterile pharmaceutical products — WHO TRS 1044, Annex 2](../sources/Sterile-Products-WHO.lingua#r_6BVEG1GSVGGGD566CJKD254DSB), the relevant transfer/barrier sections.

Model a layout with room, airlock, local process and outdoor paths. Solve pressure and mass balances before contaminant transport. Then identify a transfer event requiring more spatial or temporal detail than the steady network.

**Work:** Reproduce the two-room and counterflow examples, including reversals and zero-net-flow exchange. Compare network prediction with the assumptions and validation evidence of the moving-boundary study. Propose observations that discriminate leakage, buoyancy and motion. Defend the product, worker and neighboring-room consequences separately.

